ook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAMADA, TAKAYOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HATTORI, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI HEAVY INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUBAKI, YASUHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>BESSHO MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HAMADA TAKAYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HATTORI TOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUBAKI YASUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>BESSHO, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAMADA, TAKAYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HATTORI, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUBAKI, YASUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A produced gas produced by a decomposition reaction between an organic halogen compound and steam is neutralization-reacted with an alkali liquid and left for a preset time, and the neutralized product thus produced is precipitated in an alkali liquid for removing.  A removing pipe (71) for pumping up the entire neutralized product is allowed to project into an exhaust gas treating tank (41), a disk-like plate (71a) is fixed to the tip end of the removing pipe (71) in parallel with the bottom surface of the tank (41), and the tip end of the removing pipe (71) is opened at the center of the lower surface of the plate (71a), thereby enhancing a solid-liquid (neutralized product-alkali liquid) separation efficiency and reducing a residual amount of the alkali liquid to be disposed of along with the neutralized product as wastes.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Un gaz produit par une réaction de décomposition entre un composé halogéné organique et de la vapeur est mis à réagir par neutralisation avec un liquide alcalin et laissé pendant un temps préétabli, le produit neutralisé ainsi obtenu est précipité dans un liquide alcalin afin d'être extrait. On laisse dépasser un tube d'extraction (71) destiné au pompage de tout le produit neutralisé dans un réservoir de traitement (41) de gaz d'échappement, une plaque discoïde (71a) est fixée à la pointe du tube d'extraction (71) en parallèle à la surface du fond du réservoir (41), et la pointe du tube d'extraction (71) est ouverte au centre de la surface inférieure de la plaque (71a), activant ainsi l'efficacité de séparation solide-liquide (du produit neutralisé-liquide alcalin) et réduisant la quantité résiduelle du liquide alcalin à rejeter avec le produit neutralisé constituant les déchets.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>